attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a long spine.** Columns 0 to 20, `ampG` to `nrdR`, are carried by 94 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 0.4% of calls {S1, P}. The model names 87 to 100% of them, fewest at column 6, `yajR`, 87% {S1}.

@variable **A single variable column follows**, column 21, `yajI`, carried by 88% {S2.c21}. The spine resumes at columns 22 to 39, `tsx` to `rdgC`, and columns 41 to 50, `ppnP` to `iraP`, both carried by 92 to 95% {S3, S5}. At columns 58 to 59 a branch runs in 20 to 44%, and the `mhp` genes, columns 73 to 79, are [[hydroxy]] {S8.c58-59, S12.c73-79, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 97 against 92%, and hesitates less there, 0.17 against 0.53 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 66, `yaiP`, is a variable column, at 1.22 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork and variable columns.** Columns 73 to 79, `mhpT` to `mhpA`, are carried by 46 to 80% of chromosomes, in a region of plasticity in 58 to 86% of calls {S12, P}. The last column is `mhpA`, in 46% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 96% of genes**, 0.24 bits on average, perplexity 1.3 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.70 against 0.18 bits, and names fewer genes, 90% against 97% {C}.

